.TH DIPITVHEAD 1 "2026-08-27" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipitvhead \- re-package transport streams as a DVB-IPI multicast, with bitrate shaping, HbbTV AIT injection, and Simulcrypt/BISS scrambling
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipitvhead
.B \-i
.I uri
.RI [ per-input\ options ]
[
.B \-i
.I uri
\&...]
.RB { \-m
.IB group : port
.B |
.B \-R
.IR uri }
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipitvhead
re-packages one or more already-muxed transport streams (not raw
elementary streams) as one DVB-IPI multicast, under its own PAT/NIT
(mux-wide) and one PMT/SDT per program. A single
.B \-i
produces a normal Single Program Transport Stream (SPTS); multiple
.B \-i
produce a Multi Program Transport Stream (MPTS), one program per input,
each connected and retried independently. One input being down never
stops output for the others. No transcoding is performed.
.PP
Input sources are given with repeatable
.B \-i
flags: multicast
.RI ( udp:// ", " rtp:// ,
RTP headers stripped automatically), HTTP/HTTPS, or stdin
.RB ( \- ).
Options marked per-input below pair with the
.B \-i
immediately preceding them, ffmpeg-style; using one before any
.B \-i
is an error. Program selection within a source is automatic (first
PAT-listed program whose PMT actually arrives) unless overridden with
.BR \-p .
.PP
Output goes to a multicast group/port
.RB ( \-m ,
RTP-wrapped by default) and/or one or more bonded RIST or SRT peers
.RB ( \-R ,
requires librist or libsrt, one scheme at a time); at least one of
.B \-m
or
.B \-R
is required. Target output
bitrate can be shaped with
.BR \-b ,
combined with null-packet stuffing
.RB ( \-S )
and/or burst-limited pacing
.RB ( \-B ).
.PP
HbbTV signalling
.RB ( \-\-hbbtv )
injects an AIT (ETSI TS 102 809) advertising one AUTOSTART hybrid
broadcast/broadband application per input; this is a separate
specification from DVB-IPI itself, not a passthrough of any source AIT.
.PP
CAS scrambling is optional and mutually exclusive between families:
Simulcrypt
.RB ( \-\-cas\-algo / \-\-cas\-ecmg\-* ,
acting as SCS and EMMG-side MUX against one or more ECMG vendors) or
BISS
.RB ( \-\-biss1\-sw / \-\-biss2\-sw / \-\-biss2\-ca\-receivers ,
EBU Tech 3292): BISS1 Mode 1 (CSA1), BISS2 Mode 1/E (CISSA, static
Session Word), or BISS2 Mode CA (RSA-OAEP per-receiver entitlement).
Supported ciphers are CISSA, CSA1, and CSA2; see
.B BUGS
below for what is not implemented.
.PP
Video: MPEG-2, H.264, HEVC. Audio: MPEG-1/2 (layers 1-3), AC-3,
E-AC-3, AAC (ADTS/LATM). Subtitles: EBU teletext, DVB bitmap.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Sources (per-input)
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " " \fIuri\fR
Input source:
.BR udp:// ,
.BR rtp:// ,
.BR http:// ,
.BR https:// ,
.BR rist://@ host:port[?query] ,
.BR srt://@ host:port ,
or
.B \-
for stdin. Repeatable.
.B rist://
takes a single peer only and requires librist;
.B @
is required, since an input peer always listens. Multiple
.B \-i rist://
entries are independent programs, not a bonded stream; use
.BR dipirist (1)
as a bridge for bonded RIST input. Each RIST input costs an extra
thread beyond what other input kinds cost.
.B srt://
takes a single peer only and requires libsrt;
.B @
is required, same reason as
.BR rist:// .
No bonding or rendezvous; use
.BR dipisrt (1)
as a bridge for that. Each SRT input costs an extra thread too.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pmt\-pid " " \fIpid\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: select program by PMT PID (decimal or 0x-hex,
0x0010..0x1FFE). Default: the first live one.
.TP
.B \-\-sid \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: service_id / program_number. Default: auto-assigned,
the lowest integer not already used explicitly by another
.BR \-i .
Explicit duplicates are a startup error.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-sdt " " \fItext\fR | \fB\-\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: SDT service_name. Default: passthrough of the
source's own SDT.
.B \-
drops it; text sets our own.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-iface " " \fIiface\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: incoming multicast interface.
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-eit
For the
.B \-i
right before this: drop source EIT. Default: passed through verbatim
(SPTS) or reassembled, filtered to this program's service_id, and
merged onto the shared output EIT (MPTS).
.TP
.B \-\-strip \fIlist\fR | \fBnone\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: comma-separated list of PID classes to drop from
that source:
.B DATA
(carousels, SCTE-35, other PMT entries with an unrecognized
stream_type) and
.B ECM
(that source's own CAT/ECM/EMM passthrough). Default
.B none
(nothing dropped). Only affects what the source carried;
dipitvhead's own PAT/PMT/SDT/NIT/AIT/CAT/ECM/EMM are never touched by
this flag. Source CA/ECM passthrough is attempted only when
dipitvhead's own
.BR \-\-cas\-* /BISS
is not configured for that run.
.SS HbbTV signalling (per-input)
.TP
.B \-\-hbbtv \fIurl\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: inject an AIT signalling this HbbTV application's
entry-point URL. Default: none.
.TP
.B \-\-hbbtv\-org\-id \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: HbbTV organisation_id. Required with
.BR \-\-hbbtv .
.TP
.B \-\-hbbtv\-app\-id \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: HbbTV application_id. Required with
.BR \-\-hbbtv .
.SS RIST input (per-input)
.TP
.B \-\-rist\-profile\-in \fIsimple\fR|\fImain\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this:
.B \-i rist://
only. Default:
.BR simple .
.B main
enables PSK encryption via a
.B ?secret=
query parameter on that input's URI.
.SS SRT input (per-input)
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-passphrase\-in \fIpw\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this:
.B \-i srt://
only. Enables encryption, 10..79 chars.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-pbkeylen\-in \fI16\fR|\fI24\fR|\fI32\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: key length. Requires
.BR \-\-srt\-passphrase\-in .
Default
.BR 16 .
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-streamid\-in \fIid\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: SRT streamid. Default: none.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-packetfilter\-in \fIcfg\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: SRT packet filter config string. Default: none.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-latency\-in \fIms\fR
For the
.B \-i
right before this: SRT latency. Default: library default.
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mcast " " \fIgroup\fR:\fIport\fR
Output multicast group:port
.RI ( [ addr6 ] : port
for IPv6). Required unless
.B \-R
is given.
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-out\-iface " " \fIiface\fR
Outgoing multicast interface.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-udp
Plain UDP output. Default: RTP-wrapped. Affects
.B \-m
output only.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-ttl " " \fIn\fR
Multicast TTL / hop limit, 1..255. Default
.BR 1 .
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-rist " " \fIuri\fR
.B rist://host:port\fR[\fI?query\fR]
or
.B srt://host:port
output, bonded with any other
.B \-R
of the same scheme given, alongside
.B \-m
if given, or standalone without it.
.B \-R
is one scheme at a time; mixing
.B rist://
and
.B srt://
peers is rejected. Requires librist or libsrt. Neither RIST nor SRT
output is ever RTP-wrapped;
.B \-u
only affects
.B \-m
output.
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fIp\fR
.B simple
or
.BR main ;
.B \-R rist://
peers only. Default
.BR simple .
.TP
.B \-\-secret \fIpsk\fR
.B \-R rist://
pre-shared key. Requires
.BR \-\-profile\ main .
.TP
.B \-\-cname \fIname\fR
.B \-R rist://
RTCP cname. Default: library default.
.TP
.B \-\-buffer \fIms\fR
.B \-R rist://
recovery buffer. Default: library default.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-group\-mode \fIbroadcast\fR|\fIbackup\fR
Bonding mode across more than one
.B \-R srt://
peer. Required with more than one such peer, rejected with exactly one.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-passphrase \fIpw\fR
.B \-R srt://
encryption passphrase, 10..79 chars. Applies to every
.B \-R srt://
peer.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-pbkeylen \fI16\fR|\fI24\fR|\fI32\fR
.B \-R srt://
key length. Requires
.BR \-\-srt\-passphrase .
Default
.BR 16 .
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-streamid \fIid\fR
.B \-R srt://
streamid. Default: none.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-packetfilter \fIcfg\fR
.B \-R srt://
packet filter config string. Default: none.
.TP
.B \-\-srt\-latency \fIms\fR
.B \-R srt://
latency. Default: library default.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-nit " " \fItext\fR | \fB\-\fR
NIT for the whole output.
.B \-
drops it; text sets our own. Default: SPTS passes through the
source's own NIT if present; MPTS sends no NIT.
.SS Bitrate control
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bitrate " " \fIkbps\fR
Target output bitrate, shared across all inputs. Default: no shaping,
source rate passes straight through.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-stuff
Null-packet stuffing when output falls behind
.BR \-b 's
target. Needs
.BR \-b .
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-burst\-limit
Paces sending so output never runs ahead of
.BR \-b 's
target. Needs
.BR \-b .
Combinable with
.BR \-S .
.SS Reliability and TLS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-error " " \fIseconds\fR
On input error, reconnect after N seconds. Default: fail once and stop
(single input only); with more than one
.B \-i
every input always retries independently regardless of this flag,
defaulting to 5 seconds when
.B \-e
is not given. Output socket and continuity counters stay up across
any gap.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-insecure
Skip TLS verification (self-signed certificate, hostname, expiry).
.SS Identifiers
.TP
.B \-\-tsid \fIn\fR
transport_stream_id, 1..65535. Default
.BR 1 .
.TP
.B \-\-onid \fIn\fR
original_network_id, 1..65535. Default
.BR 1 .
.SS Logging and metrics
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
One self-updating line of stats on stderr, about once a second.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fIwhen\fR
.BR auto ", " always ", or " never .
Default
.BR auto .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics \fIpath\fR
Unix datagram socket for metrics. Default
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-id \fIname\fR
Stable instance id. Metrics are disabled unless set.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-interval \fIs\fR
Snapshot interval in seconds. Default
.BR 5 .
.SS Conditional access: Simulcrypt
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-algo \fIa\fR
Enable CAS:
.BR cissa ", " csa2 ", or " csa1 .
Default: disabled.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg \fIep\fR
ECMG address,
.BR tcp://host:port .
Repeatable, one CAS vendor per
.BR \-\-cas\-ecmg .
Required with
.BR \-\-cas\-algo .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg\-version \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: protocol version
.BR 2 " or " 3 .
Default: auto-negotiate.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-super\-id \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: Super_CAS_id, decimal or 0x-hex. Required per vendor.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-ecm\-id \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: ECM_id. Required per vendor.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-ecm\-pid \fIpid\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: output PID for its ECM stream. Default
.BR 0x0020 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-emmg\-port \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: our EMMG listener port. Default
.BR 8002 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-emmg\-max\-conns \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: max concurrent EMMG client connections, 1..64.
Default
.BR 8 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-emmg\-version \fIn\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: EMMG protocol version
.BR 2 " or " 3 .
Default: accept the client's proposal.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-emm\-pid \fIpid\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: output PID for its EMM stream. Default
.BR 0x0021 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-resilience \fIr\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: behavior on its own ECMG loss:
.BR frozen ", " cycling ", or " silent .
Default
.BR frozen .
.B frozen
keeps scrambling with the last known-good control word until the
ECMG returns.
.B cycling
keeps flipping parity on schedule between the last two known control
words instead of freezing on one.
.B silent
stops resending that vendor's ECM stream while its ECMG is
unreachable; content stays scrambled with the last known-good control
word, same as
.BR frozen .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-required
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: its outage forces the global fallback (see
.B \-\-cas\-fallback\-clear
below) regardless of other vendors.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-cwenc\-algo \fIa\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: encrypt
.BR CW_provision 's
control word per ETSI TS 103 197 Annex D. As specified,
.B des56
is supported. However, it allows extensions, so we used it as
generic as possible for some modern interpretation.
.BR des56 ", " aes128 ", or " aes256 .
Default: off (plaintext, today's behavior).
.B des56
is the spec-literal single-DES scheme. Included for interop, not as
a recommendation.
.BR aes128 " and " aes256
are a generic extension of the same Annex D parameter framing.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-cwenc\-aes\-mode \fIm\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this:
.BR stream " or " ecb ,
.BR aes128 / aes256
only. Default
.BR stream .
.B ecb
is rejected when this vendor's control word is 8 bytes (AES has no
8-byte block mode).
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-cwenc\-fixed\-key \fIhex\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: fixed key, hex-encoded:
14 chars for
.BR des56 ,
32 for
.BR aes128 ,
64 for
.BR aes256 .
Default: for
.BR des56 ,
Annex D's own published ROM key; no default for
.BR aes128 / aes256 ,
which fail at startup instead if a key list is not configured either.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-cwenc\-key\-list\-a \fIpath\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: Annex D key list file, exactly 2048 raw bytes.
Either this or
.B \-\-cas\-cwenc\-fixed\-key
selects the key addressing mode used per
.BR CW_provision .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-cwenc\-key\-list\-b \fIpath\fR
For the
.B \-\-cas\-ecmg
right before this: second Annex D key list file, same format as
.BR \-\-cas\-cwenc\-key\-list\-a .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-pids \fIlist\fR
PIDs to scramble: comma-separated output-side PIDs (decimal or
0x-hex) and/or the
.B video
/
.B audio
keywords, meaning every video/audio elementary stream on the output.
Freely mixable, e.g.
.BR 0x0103,video .
Default
.B video,audio
(all video and audio streams). Content is scrambled exactly once
regardless of vendor count; also used, with the same default, under
any BISS mode below.
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-cp\-duration \fIms\fR
Crypto-period duration in milliseconds, 1..86400000, shared by every
vendor. Default
.BR 10000 .
.TP
.B \-\-cas\-fallback\-clear
On total outage (every vendor down, or a
.B \-\-cas\-required
vendor down specifically): go clear-to-air instead of staying
scrambled on the last known-good control word.
.SS Conditional access: BISS
.TP
.B \-\-biss1\-sw \fIhex12\fR
Enable legacy BISS1 Mode 1: 12 hex char Session Word, scrambles with
CSA1. BISS1 Mode E (DES) is not supported. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-biss2\-sw / \-\-cas\-algo .
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-sw \fIhex32\fR
Enable BISS2 Mode 1/E: 32 hex char Session Word, scrambles with CISSA.
No ECMG/EMMG. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-cas\-algo .
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-emit\-esw \fIid\fR
With
.BR \-\-biss2\-sw :
log the AES-128-ECB Encrypted Session Word for this 32 hex char receiver
ID, for out-of-band distribution.
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-ca\-receivers \fIdir\fR
Enable BISS2 Mode CA (EBU Tech 3292-s1): directory of PKCS#8 PEM
public keys, one per entitled receiver/group. Rescanned on
.BR SIGHUP ;
a receiver removed from the directory is revoked, forcing an
immediate Session Key change. Requires
.B \-\-cas\-cp\-duration
of at least 1000 (T_ECM_change_min); the Session Key rotates every
6th Session Word period. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-biss1\-sw / \-\-biss2\-sw / \-\-cas\-algo .
.TP
.B \-\-biss2\-ca\-session\-id \fIn\fR
Administratively unique entitlement_session_id, decimal or 0x-hex,
16-bit. Default: random at startup.
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH PID ALLOCATION
Mux-wide, fixed, shared by every program (DVB-SI reserved range,
ETSI EN 300 468): PAT
.BR 0x0000 ,
NIT
.BR 0x0010 ,
SDT
.BR 0x0011 ,
EIT
.BR 0x0012 ,
CAT
.BR 0x0001 .
.PP
Every other table is per-program, in a fixed 32-PID block keyed to
that input's 0-based position (i) among the
.B \-i
flags: PMT 0x1000+i, video 0x0100+i*32, other elementary streams
0x0101+i*32 upward in discovery order, AIT 0x011F+i*32. A single
.B \-i
is i=0, identical to before per-program blocks existed.
.SH MULTIPLE INPUTS (MPTS)
More than one
.B \-i
produces an MPTS. Servicing is one poll loop, not one thread per
input, taken in round-robin order so no input is always serviced
last; each input is capped at 32 TS packets read per tick so one busy
source can't starve the others that tick. There is no de-jitter
buffering beyond that.
.PP
Each program keeps forwarding its own source's PCR untouched. There
is no synthesized mux-wide clock, so a program's timing stays
accurate to its own source regardless of what the others are doing.
.PP
The per-program elementary-stream cap is 31 real streams, one slot
always reserved for AIT whether
.B \-\-hbbtv
is used on that input or not. Extras beyond that are dropped in
discovery order, logged once per program setup.
.PP
It is one process, one thread doing the demux/remux/CAS work for
every program on a running instance. Capacity is a CPU budget
question, not a thread or connection limit; plan program count per
instance, and instance count per host, with that in mind.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
CAS support is a build-time option
.RI ( DIPITVHEAD_CAS ,
on by default). CISSA needs OpenSSL. CSA1, CSA2, and BISS1 dlopen
.I libdvbcsa
at runtime if present; dipitvhead is not built against it and does
not bundle it, and static release tarballs do not contain it either.
RIST input/output needs
.IR librist ,
SRT input/output needs
.IR libsrt ,
same as every other tool in this toolkit. HTTPS input is a
build-time option too
.RI ( \-DDIPITVHEAD_TLS=OFF ,
auto-off without OpenSSL). Missing any of these degrades that
feature to unavailable, not a build failure.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Stop.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Re-read the BISS2 Mode CA receivers directory
.RB ( \-\-biss2\-ca\-receivers )
and apply any added, removed, or changed keys.
.SH BUGS
CISSA, CSA1, CSA2, BISS1 Mode 1, BISS2 Mode 1/E, and BISS2 Mode CA
only; no CSA3, no BISS1 Mode E (DES). BISS2 Mode CA: one keypair per
file in the receivers directory, no group key pairs; no
entitlement_priv_data_loop vendor extensions;
prevent_descrambled_forward/prevent_decoded_forward/insert_watermark
entitlement flags are always 0 (unenforced). Single-pass scrambler
only, no re-scrambling of already-scrambled input.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-m 239.1.1.1:5000 \-s "My Channel"
Basic SPTS: one RTP source re-streamed with its own SDT service name.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i https://host/live/x/y.ts \-k \-m 239.1.1.2:5000 \-b 8000 \-S \-B
HTTPS source with a self-signed certificate, bitrate-shaped to
8000 kbps with stuffing and burst limiting.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-\-sdt "Channel A" \-i rtp://@239.19.75.2:8700 \-\-sdt "Channel B" \-m 239.1.1.3:5000 \-e 5
MPTS: two RTP sources merged into one output, each its own program,
5-second reconnect on input error.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i udp://@239.0.0.1:5000 \-m 239.5.5.5:6000 \-\-hbbtv https://example.org/hbbtv/ \-\-hbbtv\-org\-id 1 \-\-hbbtv\-app\-id 100
Inject an HbbTV AUTOSTART application AIT alongside the program.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-m 239.1.1.1:5000 \-\-cas\-algo cissa \-\-cas\-ecmg tcp://ecmg.example:2222 \-\-cas\-super\-id 0x4A750002 \-\-cas\-ecm\-id 1
Scramble an SPTS via Simulcrypt CISSA against one ECMG vendor.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-m 239.1.1.1:5000 \-\-biss2\-sw 00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff
BISS2 Mode 1/E: static 32 hex char Session Word, no ECMG/EMMG needed.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-m 239.1.1.1:5000 \-\-biss1\-sw 0123456789ab
Legacy BISS1 Mode 1: 12 hex char Session Word, CSA1.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-m 239.1.1.1:5000 \-\-biss2\-ca\-receivers /etc/biss\-ca/receivers
BISS2 Mode CA: per-receiver RSA entitlement, one PEM pubkey per file
under the directory.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-R rist://recv1.example:2000 \-R rist://recv2.example:2000 \-\-profile main \-\-secret s3cr3t12345
RIST output bonded to two peers, PSK-encrypted.
.TP
.B dipitvhead \-i rtp://@239.19.75.1:8700 \-R srt://recv.example:9000 \-\-srt\-passphrase s3cr3t12345
SRT output to a single peer, encrypted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
Non-zero on argument errors or I/O/network failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipiradiohead (1),
.BR dipimetrics (1),
.BR dipirist (1),
